[{:db/id "q-333696/field-1/f8a9b97247a5ac35092ebd2fe07df2589fbf183484eeacb8d7c413bf9bf0d19a" :answer/id #uuid "a5929aa8-1ec4-5434-86d0-a4da0128686f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10e^t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333696/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0ecbd4b-860d-55f4-aa0d-dbdbba9ee788" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333696/field-1/f8a9b97247a5ac35092ebd2fe07df2589fbf183484eeacb8d7c413bf9bf0d19a" :answer-field/choices ["q-333696/field-1/f8a9b97247a5ac35092ebd2fe07df2589fbf183484eeacb8d7c413bf9bf0d19a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333696" :question/id #uuid "2d193e39-56b8-5f6e-821e-907d61fea31a" :question/math-academy-id "q-333696" :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t}\\cdot 5{e}^{-2t}-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =10{e}^{3t-2t} \\\\  & =10{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333696/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b4d9d68-59b6-5209-8265-e1e062c422bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333696"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333728/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "70bb9d8d-b1b0-5cfb-be12-b00397021225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333728/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "546c2a08-8373-58c3-abc8-d25ab8e85f12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333728/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac8f17d9-4e3c-5590-8ff2-6a3a83746548" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333728/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-333728/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-333728/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333728" :question/id #uuid "e2de35bb-a108-571f-91e9-0b0c6ae84ae3" :question/math-academy-id "q-333728" :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t+1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}t+1 & t-1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(t+1)\\cdot 2-(t-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2t+2-2t+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333728/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b4d9d68-59b6-5209-8265-e1e062c422bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333728"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322731/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "230acb2e-2d20-5198-91a6-b3f7968c51b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220060 :answer-field/correct "q-322731/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-322731/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-322731"] :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3t) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-333704/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1b5cb571-dec9-5e2b-88f4-e25b2de5e68c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333704/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4d680a26-1b66-5871-9164-3054597dcda9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333704/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8168ad25-49f4-5d4f-bf53-1d8be92323af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333704/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-333704/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-333704/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333704" :question/id #uuid "f53fdfca-0e3d-56d4-a5f5-6d1de3cc44e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-333704" :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ t\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+1 & t \\\\ t & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+1)\\cdot 1-t\\cdot t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333704/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b4d9d68-59b6-5209-8265-e1e062c422bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333704"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333695/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d3220c96-5862-5f94-82ed-83c5018994f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220466 :answer-field/correct "q-333695/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-333695/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-333695"] :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe Wronskian of the vector-valued functions given above is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & ={e}^{t-t} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-352424/field-1/a28c07e093cbb47dba4e0f7de239aa1dc43e6df0eaa50ee8374be23c9913672e" :answer/id #uuid "d5153b3d-0967-5b43-8df8-bd50cd4c8434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10{e}^{6t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352424/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7be