(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- If the Wronskian is not identically zero, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly independent.\n\n- If the Wronskian is identically zero, and it's known that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are solutions to the same system of linear ODEs, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIn our case, our Wronskian is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{2t}-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & ={e}^{4t} \\\\  & ={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is $\\text{nonzero for at least one }t\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the set ${{x}_{1}(t),{x}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly $\\text{independent}$ on $R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333741/field-1" "q-333741/field-2" "q-333741/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee461d3e-3afa-51c6-bddd-355668cac3ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333741"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333895/field-1/6350861b7e3b40a68ee9b7c75edc31888678d87a82ba7502716e6479dc0d865f" :answer/id #uuid "f7375b9a-9a2e-56bd-880a-7b3be141fa56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+9{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333895/field-1/1b32b10818445277961589c9c7692da18cd19ad109a07c131b6f4d662f1e7353" :answer/id #uuid "ed55b08a-1272-5331-be00-79bf8e3f5d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333895/field-1/2a5ce277f78ff05921a5c08b3352fec61760b298fcebca21139fb40733b68f22" :answer/id #uuid "cc4a1672-4daf-56d2-ac73-9fe227ee3adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(