1" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-322737/field-5/b49703179306e83d85bbe4c6ac62481c17882ef850059eeb30e83821a2dfad88" :answer-field/choices ["q-322737/field-5/a5293ac7e38dfeb2fca32f5db893dfe7d07d9fede1ba2b4be5e824acba2ca866" "q-322737/field-5/b49703179306e83d85bbe4c6ac62481c17882ef850059eeb30e83821a2dfad88" "q-322737/field-5/1c2bd59983d2c1fb302dc9e16af330828afdf644688012d6ce01f41ba68c277a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322737/field-6/64a58b55bd5395a70e437bad4cc044d49f6752b09ddfbfa022d212ab174018c0" :answer/id #uuid "6604d079-1fa4-5548-a15b-700490d300e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322737/field-6/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b1db3204-9c97-5ded-b301-c8cc04a9a767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322737/field-6/a1ebd2482f5be58f7e4d544dab368c68ef21eb68b1b06c10c7f2bdd815b52cfb" :answer/id #uuid "bd99a357-3b80-5d1b-b3ba-d7c80c32979a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322737/field-6/ee7f30284a149c61b599f73a98c2926019642343afb3d5728e334f85bf1de76b" :answer/id #uuid "13d9e56f-bde9-5f48-868e-3d246b8a8970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{e}^{-3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322737/field-6" :answer-field/id #uuid "05127a3c-f46d-5057-9a05-d33b50bcc822" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-322737/field-6/ee7f30284a149c61b599f73a98c2926019642343afb3d5728e334f85bf1de76b" :answer-field/choices ["q-322737/field-6/64a58b55bd5395a70e437bad4cc044d49f6752b09ddfbfa022d212ab174018c0" "q-322737/field-6/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-322737/field-6/a1ebd2482f5be58f7e4d544dab368c68ef21eb68b1b06c10c7f2bdd815b52cfb" "q-322737/field-6/ee7f30284a149c61b599f73a98c2926019642343afb3d5728e334f85bf1de76b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-322737"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs above, where $t\\in R.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below. $\\,$ The function $a(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]$ \n{{field-1}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $b(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ \n{{field-2}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $c(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ \n{{field-3}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ {{field-4}} \nis a set of fundamental solutions to the system because the Wronskian \n\n$$\nW({{field-5}})={{field-6}}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n$\\,$ for at least one $t\\in R.$" :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- If the Wronskian is not identically zero, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly independent.\n\n- If the Wronskian is identically zero, and it's known that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are solutions to the same system of linear ODEs, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nFirst, we write our system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute the given vectors into the matrix differential equation:\n\n- $a(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]$ $\\text{is}$ a solution of the system. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}(7{e}^{-4t})^{′} \\\\ (2{e}^{-4t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-28{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -8{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6\\cdot 7{e}^{-4t}+7\\cdot 2{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -2\\cdot 7{e}^{-4t}+3\\cdot 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-28{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -8{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-28{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -8{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $b(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ $\\text{isn't}$ a solution of the system. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}({e}^{t})^{′} \\\\ (-2{e}^{t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6\\cdot {e}^{t}+7\\cdot (-2{e}^{t}) \\\\ -2\\cdot {e}^{t}+3\\cdot (-2{e}^{t})\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-20{e}^{t} \\\\ -8{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $c(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ $\\text{is}$ a solution of the system. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}({e}^{t})^{′} \\\\ ({e}^{t})^{′}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6\\cdot {e}^{t}+7\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\ -2\\cdot {e}^{t}+3\\cdot {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, consider the set of solutions ${a,c}.$ Its Wronskian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(a,c) & =|\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-4t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(7{e}^{-4t})\\cdot {e}^{t}-{e}^{t}\\cdot 2{e}^{-4t} \\\\  & =7{e}^{-3t}-2{e}^{-3t} \\\\  & =5{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is nonzero for at least one $t\\in R.$ Thus, since $a$ and $c$ are both solutions of the same linear system, and their Wronskian is nonzero for at least one $t\\in R,$ ${a,c}$ is a set of fundamental solutions of the system." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-322737/field-4" "q-322737/field-5" "q-322737/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334527/field-1/61af73b8e8ead9835a9b9a8e325b35ee392bbd1ef8d56b833ee0389146eb9f6a" :answer/id #uuid "1ebc8c8c-9b65-5c25-bf95-5f424654f2f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "isn't" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334527/field-1/d029defaf49fa0f42d047edac2d8d14ec0638f11d1f3b80a99f458177dd8f219" :answer/id #uuid "4efdaf34-187e-599d-aa2f-03974e5eba31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334527/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b227797a-4497-599d-a505-a3619c11efe9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334527/field-1/d029defaf49fa0f42d047edac2d8d14ec0638f11d1f3b80a99f458177dd8f219" :answer-field/choices ["q-334527/field-1/61af73b8e8ead9835a9b9a8e325b35ee392bbd1ef8d56b833ee0389146eb9f6a" "q-334527/field-1/d029defaf49fa0f42d047edac2d8d14ec0638f11d1f3b80a99f458177dd8f219"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334527/field-2/d029defaf49fa0f42d047edac2d8d14ec0638f11d1f3b80a99f458177dd8f219" :answer/id #uuid "d0662b1b-5958-548b-9f19-ae40f2e39048" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334527/field-2/61af73b8e8ead9835a9b9a8e325b35ee392bbd1ef8d56b833ee0389146eb9f6a" :answer/id #uuid "d0dacbbf-a43d-50a8-86e7-3d6004a43499" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "isn't" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334527/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3fb4f89d-d2a6-5716-817d-555d213f3206